From: Herman Brule <brule.herman@confiared.com>
Subject: udebug: no ring without udebugd

Only udebugd reads a ring. Without it procd, netifd and logd still mapped six
96 KB rings that filled page by page: 576 KB of Shmem on a 32 MB ONU, read by
nobody. udebug_buf_init now keeps no ring when /usr/sbin/udebugd is absent; the
entry functions already return early on a ring with no header, and
udebug_buf_free now does too.

--- a/udebug.c	2026-10-18 18:47:26.594320676 -0400
+++ b/udebug.c	2026-10-18 18:47:26.605474550 -0400
@@ -457,6 +457,10 @@
 
 	udebug_init_page_size();
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&buf->list);
+	/* only udebugd reads a ring: without it, keep no RAM for one */
+	if (access("/usr/sbin/udebugd", X_OK))
+		return -1;
+
 	if (size < page_size)
 		size = page_size;
 	while(size > 1U << order)
@@ -682,6 +686,9 @@
 {
 	struct udebug *ctx = buf->ctx;
 
+	if (!buf->hdr)
+		return;
+
 	if (!list_empty(&buf->list) && buf->list.prev)
 		list_del(&buf->list);
 
